  "note": "Dates transcribed (not computed) from the Government of India DoPT office memoranda \"Holidays to be observed in Central Government Offices during the year YYYY\": Annexure I (compulsory/gazetted holidays for Delhi/New Delhi administrative offices) and Annexure II (restricted holidays). \"list\" is \"gazetted\" when the festival is in Annexure I, else \"restricted\". Where DoPT later changed a date by corrigendum/OM (moon-sighting changes etc.) the corrected date is used and the change is cited in \"memo\". dussehra is the gazetted Vijaya Dashami row; diwali is the gazetted \"Diwali (Deepavali)\" row; janmashtami prefers the gazetted (Vaishnava) row when a separate RH Smarta date also exists. Where a festival appears twice in one year's list (Islamic festivals occurring twice in a Gregorian year), the first occurrence is recorded. navratri_start is recorded only where a dated row explicitly names \"1st Navratra\" (2027 only, in the combined RH row \"Chaitra Sukladi/Gudi Padava/Ugadi/Cheti Chand/1st Navratra\"). source_kind \"dopt_pdf\" covers DoPT originals on documents.doptcirculars.nic.in / dopt.gov.in, DoPT's own HTML copies (2002, 2003) and web.archive.org captures of the persmin.nic.in originals (2004, 2007, 2008). Years 2000, 2001, 2005 and 2006 could not be sourced and are omitted. 2002: Holi has no numbered Annexure I row; Annexure I carries the footnote \"Holi - 29th March - holiday on account of Good Friday\", recorded as gazetted.",
